  "per_ability_observations": {
    "kodanda": [
      "The sampled arm raise, single projectile path, target impact cue and later ready pose are coherent at this camera. Ammunition remains 11/12 after the one accepted shot.",
      "No gross silhouette tear or new cape fan is observed in the inspected windows. Fingers, string attachment and subtle cloth lag are not resolved well enough for fine-contact approval."
    ],
    "piercing_dawn": [
      "The gold lane warning and open curved solar-seal motifs precede the released projectile; sampled impact cues appear at the staged line of receivers. Warning geometry clears on release, and later sampled expiry frames have no lingering projectile effect.",
      "The low-angle still supports costume/bow outline and open-centre VFX readability. The three source-authored arc groups overlap/occlude at this scale, so a complete three-lobe shape-quality pass is not inferred from a count."
    ],
    "measured_step": [
      "The blue curved movement trail accompanies forward displacement in the player camera and clears by the later sampled return-to-ready state.",
      "Adjacent poses maintain a recognizable cape/leg outline, with no newly observed gross explosion or tear. This short sample does not establish grounded foot friction, collision counterplay or complete locomotion blending."
    ],
    "guardian_circle": [
      "The radius boundary and broad mint curves distinguish the field during windup, release and active recovery. The HUD shows released, then field active with visible shield/healing values.",
      "At frame270 the boundary and active field label remain. At271/272 the visible boundary is absent and the HUD reads Rama is ready; recorded authority age is5.05 s, main/recipient opacity0 and recipient surfaces0. Cast data is later disposed at280. The field-object tail is not mistaken for ongoing active presentation.",
      "The foreground field is large at this camera and shares pale values with the paving; crowded-match visual clarity needs a separate test. Reduced-effects still preserves its radius/readability, but one still cannot establish reduced-motion temporal behavior."
    ],
    "dawn_volley": [
      "Three lane warnings and open curved sun-blade motifs gather before released arrows; sampled receiver impact cues appear and later expiry frames return to a clear ready scene.",
      "The three source-authored blade groups have an open centre in these views, but they partially overlap behind/around the hero. Normal-speed choreography and fine curve/attachment quality remain LIMITED."
    ]
  },
